repository-code: 'https://github.com/USEPA/dmapSMP/'
abstract: >-
  The dmapSMP Shade Model Preprocessing tool is a process
  that prepares NHDPlus High Resolution (HR) flowline
  datasets for processing in RShade
  (https://github.com/USEPA/dmap-RShade) which in turn can
  generate estimates of topographic and vegetative shade at
  equally spaced intervals along a stream network. dmapSMP
  does this by taking the spatial data, calculating new
  columns, and exporting to a csv that can be input directly
  into RShade.
